the Academy nickel fellowship has  enormous significance for me as a  screenwriter and as a governor of the  screenwriters branch of the Academy the  Academy has 17 branches but ours is the  only branch with a dedicated fellowship  that allows us to extend a hand to the  next generation of emerging artists in  our field it's an incredible privilege  the existence of the nickel fellowships  attest to the facts that writing is  foundational to cinema those of us on  the nickel committee believe that the  importance of mentorship in young  Raiders cannot be overstated and I can  really speak for my own haphazard  experience when I broke into the film  business in nineteen eighty i was  completely clueless about the art and  the business of screenwriting i was from  a small town in the south and I went to  New York seeking a way to make movies I  kept my day job there while I was still  trying to teach myself to write at night  and on weekends and I knocked on a lot  of doors in New York looking for a way  into filmmaking after really zero  success two things finally happened some  friends and I put on a small fringe  production of a play that I had written  on off off Broadway in the basement of  the Ansonia hotel and an agent  small-time agent who was working on her  own saw the play and suggested that I  try writing for film when I gave her a  screenplay but I was working on and  somehow she managed to sell it that was  how I got in at the time there was  really very few female screenwriters  working in Hollywood I was so hungry for  a mentor and so keen to try and  understand filmmaking better that I used  to just cold approach film editors at  screenings and so forth and asked if I  could sit in their editing rooms only  one editor gave me permission it was  Susan from key who was cutting  documentaries for the mazal brothers but  it was by this kind of trial and error  that I began to learn the rules and  conventions of cinematic narrative and  how to navigate the film industry what  the nickel fellowship does is open the  door to writers who are working on their  own and looking for a way to enter the  professional world to filmmaking because  the nickel committee and our team of  readers is drawn from every branch of  the Academy  the nickel fellowship actually allows  everyone in the Academy to serve as  mentors for this emerging writers it's a  community effort the Academy nickel  fellowships carries a generous cash  prize which is a huge boost for writer  getting her start when I wrote my first  screenplay I was using a friend's borrow  typewriter so it cash really makes a  difference but perhaps more important  than the prize money is just the simple  acknowledgment by the Academy that we  believe in the work of these writers who  are being honored tonight and we will  back you with all of the resources that  the Academy has to offer this past  weekend the governor's awards the  Academy honored screenwriter jean-claude  carrière with an honorary Oscar kind of  a lifetime achievement award jean-claude  who has elevated screenwriting to the  level of literature through his work on  more than 130 films sat on Saturday that  too often screenwriters go unnoticed and  are like shadows passing through the  history of cinema we want to be sure  that that doesn't happen to these  incredibly talented writers who are  among this year's finalists and winners  over these years the Academy over the  years that the fellowship has been in  existence the Academy has received more  than 130,000 script submissions for the  fellowship that's a lot is replaced the  writers have gone on to win prizes and  accolades around the world and I have to  say that this year's winners have  emerged from a pretty competitive pack  one question I often hear about the  nickel fellowship is who reads all those  scripts well more people than ever now  have to dedicate their time to reviewing  the submissions and making  recommendations this year's crop was  read by more than 200 Academy member  volunteers 45 of them have been one have  one or have been nominated for Academy  Awards during their careers pretty  high-class bunch so i have to say thank  you to them for giving their time  and I want to thank the rest of the  Academy nickel committee who poured over  the finalists scripts and engaged in a  very spirited discussion before we  arrived at this year's list of honorees  I don't think that there is a more  accomplished group of judges anywhere so  with the nickel committee members who  are here tonight please stand  I would like to congratulate last year's  fellows who were able to join us tonight  Frank to John David hedges you guys can  stand up patty Jones Alan Ross Stephanie  Shannon Barbra Stefanski I hope you had  a great fellowship here and I cannot  wait to see your movies we are also  really lucky to have with us tonight  some past fellows who wrote or directed  films that were in release or word  festivals this past year there is life  after the nickel anthony jaswinski here  what Christie Eric eryn krueger who  wrote transformers age of extinction  James modern who directed by the gun and  Rebecca's son and shine who's a writer  producer on the Vampire Diaries  fantastic so before we begin our  readings tonight let's just take a  moment to thank the three casting  directors who gave their time to bring  us an excellent cast we could not have  done this without the help of David  Rubin Bernie Telsey + lure Kennedy and  of course with the help of Dina Michelle  we are really lucky to have a casting  branch now thank you Mary Jane for  feeding us thank you dawn Hudson for  your continual support and now it is my  pleasure to introduce you yeah introduce  to you the host of tonight's ceremony  who is the director of Albert Nobbs the  writer director of mother and child one  of my favorite directors Rodrigo Garcia
 

